00:07:34,950 --> 00:07:42,976
Bob Dole and George McGovern who gave us the Nancy working with Ted Kennedy to solve really big problems.
鲍勃·多尔和乔治·麦戈文为我们提供了南希与特德·肯尼迪合作解决真正大问题的机会。

136
00:07:43,170 --> 00:07:44,410
That's how it's supposed to be.
事情就应该这样。

137
00:07:44,890 --> 00:07:45,930
I'm going to tell you a little secret.
我要告诉你一个小秘密。

138
00:07:46,370 --> 00:07:48,250
I want to become Jerry Moran's best friend.
我想成为杰里·莫兰最好的朋友。

139
00:07:48,970 --> 00:07:56,535
I'm going to do everything I can for us to model for the rest of the United States States in deeply red Kansas,
我将尽我所能为我们在深红色的堪萨斯州为美国其他地区做模特，

140
00:07:56,710 --> 00:07:57,490
The heart of America.
美国的心脏。

141
00:07:57,870 --> 00:08:03,170
I want us to model what it looks like when thoughtful people actually work together to solve problems instead of slinging mud at each Other.
我希望我们能够模拟，当有思想的人们真正共同努力解决问题而不是相互指责时的样子其他。

142
00:08:03,610 --> 00:08:07,067
And instead of deciding, you know, who's going to get the credit You've heard this before.
你知道，而不是决定谁将获得荣誉，你以前听过这个。

143
00:08:07,350 --> 00:08:09,530
You can a whole lot done if you don't care who gets the credit.
如果你不在乎谁获得功劳，你可以做很多事情。

144
00:08:09,801 --> 00:08:09,996
Right?
正确的？

145
00:08:10,130 --> 00:08:11,657
We're going to be that kind of state.
我们将成为那样的状态。

146
00:08:12,297 --> 00:08:14,450
Now, the second thing is decency.
现在，第二件事是礼貌。

147
00:08:15,605 --> 00:08:18,630
And when I think about what does decency look like, I think about Matthew 7:12.
当我想到什么是正派时，我就会想到马太福音 7 章 12 节。

148
00:08:18,630 --> 00:08:20,330
I want you to finish this for me if you will.
如果你愿意的话，我希望你能帮我完成这件事。

149
00:08:20,430 --> 00:08:21,310
You learned it from your grandma.
你是从你奶奶那里学来的。

150
00:08:21,890 --> 00:08:25,087
Do unto others as you would do unto you.
己所不欲，勿施于人。

151
00:08:25,087 --> 00:08:25,830
Yeah, you all do that.
是的，你们都这样做。

152
00:08:25,930 --> 00:08:26,870
You see it in every religion.
你在每个宗教中都能看到它。

153
00:08:27,090 --> 00:08:29,787
It's in Matthew chapter 7 verse 12 in the Sermon on the Mount.
这是马太福音第 7 章第 12 节登山宝训中的内容。

154
00:08:29,890 --> 00:08:31,747
Do unto others as you'd have them do unto you.
己所不欲，勿施于人。

155
00:08:31,747 --> 00:08:33,750
What does it look like in Washington if they actually did that?
如果他们真的这么做了，华盛顿会是什么样子？

156
00:08:34,110 --> 00:08:37,310
How would our policies and our politics change if we treated people this way?
如果我们这样对待人民，我们的政策和政治会发生什么变化？

157
00:08:37,310 --> 00:08:38,436
Or I think about Micah 6:8.
或者我想到弥迦书 6:8。

158
00:08:38,770 --> 00:08:41,570
You don't have to believe in God to find this verse very powerful.
你不必相信上帝就会发现这节经文非常强大。

159
00:08:41,690 --> 00:08:45,260
But the prophet says to his people, what does the Lord require of you?
但先知对他的子民说，主对你们有什么要求？

160
00:08:45,260 --> 00:08:48,430
Not what does he suggest, what does he require of you, but to do justice.
不是他建议什么，他对你有什么要求，而是要伸张正义。

161
00:08:48,910 --> 00:08:51,850
Justice is is fairness for people who are powerless.
正义是对弱者的公平。

162
00:08:51,850 --> 00:08:55,930
To do justice, to love kindness, and to walk humbly before God.
行公义、好仁慈、谦卑地行走在神面前。

163
00:08:56,150 --> 00:08:56,300
Right?
正确的？

164
00:08:56,570 --> 00:08:59,450
I mean, these are attributes that everybody needs to model in our world.
我的意思是，这些是我们世界中每个人都需要塑造的属性。

165
00:09:00,030 --> 00:09:02,670
I think about something that Jesus said in Matthew 25.
我想起耶稣在马太福音 25 章中所说的话。

166
00:09:02,670 --> 00:09:03,930
He was describing the Last Judgment.
他正在描述最后的审判。

167
00:09:03,930 --> 00:09:05,616
He said, here's how it's going to go down in the end.
他说，这就是最终的结局。

168
00:09:05,910 --> 00:09:10,050
I'm going to look at all of you and I'm going to say this to those who are the sheep.
我会看着你们所有人，然后对那些羊们说这些。

169
00:09:10,190 --> 00:09:12,990
I'm going to say to you, I was hungry and you gave me something to eat.
我要对你说，我饿了，你给了我吃的。

170
00:09:13,510 --> 00:09:15,590
I was thirsty and you gave me something to drink.
我渴了，你给了我喝的东西。

171
00:09:16,130 --> 00:09:18,350
I was a stranger and the Greek word is immigrant actually.
我是一个陌生人，希腊词实际上是移民。

172
00:09:18,350 --> 00:09:19,970
I was a stranger and you welcomed me.
我是一个陌生人，而你欢迎我。

173
00:09:20,270 --> 00:09:21,690
I was naked and you clothed me.
我赤身露体，你给我穿了衣服。

174
00:09:21,690 --> 00:09:23,870
I was sick and in prison and you visited me.
我生病了，在监狱里，你来看望了我。

175
00:09:23,870 --> 00:09:27,110
And as much as you've done it for the least of these, you've done it for me.
尽管你为其中最微不足道的事情做了这件事，但你也是为我做的。

176
00:09:27,210 --> 00:09:28,330
That's what decency looks like.
这就是正派的样子。

177
00:09:28,410 --> 00:09:30,850
I had a man in Holton, Kansas say to me a couple of months ago.
几个月前，堪萨斯州霍尔顿的一个人对我说。

178
00:09:30,950 --> 00:09:33,471
He said, hey preacher, I'm a one-issue voter.
他说，嘿，牧师，我是一名单一议题选民。

179
00:09:33,471 --> 00:09:35,451
And I'm like, great, tell me your one issue.
我想，太好了，告诉我你的一个问题。

180
00:09:36,097 --> 00:09:38,830
He said, I refuse to vote for anybody who doesn't believe.
他说，我拒绝投票给任何不相信的人。

181
00:09:39,756 --> 00:09:41,087
And then he paused.
然后他停了下来。

182
00:09:41,087 --> 00:09:45,383
I refuse to vote for anybody who doesn't believe that we should love our neighbor as we love ourselves.
我拒绝投票给任何不相信我们应该像爱自己一样爱邻居的人。

183
00:09:46,230 --> 00:09:47,531
That's decency.
这就是礼貌。

184
00:09:47,541 --> 00:09:54,340
Now listen, this kind of decency doesn't belittle people.
听着，这种礼貌并不贬低人。

185
00:09:54,960 --> 00:09:57,340
It doesn't benefit the rich at the expense of the poor.
它不会以牺牲穷人为代价来造福富人。

186
00:09:57,540 --> 00:09:59,408
It doesn't ignore the cries of the needy.
它不会忽视有需要的人的呼声。

187
00:09:59,520 --> 00:10:01,480
It's not cruel or unkind.
这并不残忍或不友善。

188
00:10:02,540 --> 00:10:07,149
Now when you speak of loving your neighbors as you love yourself, I want to remind you of a passage of scripture in the
现在，当您谈到爱邻居如爱自己时，我想提醒您圣经中的一段经文

189
00:10:07,149 --> 00:10:08,320
Gospel of Luke chapter 10.
路加福音第10章。

190
00:10:08,659 --> 00:10:09,800
This is 25 through 37.
这是 25 到 37。

191
00:10:09,918 --> 00:10:13,500
I've preached this passage dozens of times in the last 38 years as a pastor.
在过去 38 年的牧师生涯中，我已经多次宣讲过这段经文。

192
00:10:13,534 --> 00:10:17,100
There was a lawyer who approached Jesus and some pastor Scott preached on this not long ago.
不久前，有一位律师来找耶稣，斯科特牧师也曾宣讲过这一点。

193
00:10:17,100 --> 00:10:20,480
There was a lawyer who approached Jesus and said, what must I do to inherit eternal life?
有一位律法师来问耶稣，我必须做什么才能承受永生？

194
00:10:20,900 --> 00:10:22,400
And Jesus said, you're a religious leader.
耶稣说，你是一位宗教领袖。

195
00:10:22,720 --> 00:10:23,100
What do you think?
你怎么认为？

196
00:10:23,860 --> 00:10:26,940
And he said, love God with all your heart, soul, strength, and mind,
他说，要尽心、尽性、尽力、尽意地爱神，

197
00:10:27,500 --> 00:10:28,740
And love your neighbor as you love yourself.
并像爱自己一样爱你的邻居。

198
00:10:28,900 --> 00:10:29,700
And Jesus said, that's right.
耶稣说，没错。

199
00:10:29,800 --> 00:10:32,588
Go and do likewise or go and do this and you'll live.
去做同样的事情或者去做这个，你就会活下去。

200
00:10:32,588 --> 00:10:33,880
But then the man followed up with a question.
但随后那人又提出了一个问题。

201
00:10:34,798 --> 00:10:37,760
And he said, yeah, but Jesus, who is my neighbor?
他说，是的，但是天哪，谁是我的邻居？

202
00:10:38,780 --> 00:10:41,580
And you know what he was asking was, tell me who I don't have to love.
你知道他问的是什么，告诉我我不必爱谁。

203
00:10:42,598 --> 00:10:42,797
Right?
正确的？

204
00:10:42,797 --> 00:10:46,180
I just want to know I can love these people, but who don't I have to love?
我只是想知道我可以爱这些人，但我不必爱谁呢？

205
00:10:46,740 --> 00:10:51,340
And that's when Jesus tells a story that all of you have heard before or at least you know the title of it.
就在那时，耶稣讲述了一个你们以前都听过的故事，或者至少你们知道它的标题。

206
00:10:51,640 --> 00:10:55,000
The story of the parable of the good Samaritan.
好撒玛利亚人的寓言故事。

207
00:10:55,240 --> 00:10:55,500
All right.
好的。

208
00:10:55,760 --> 00:11:00,720
He said there was a certain man going from Jerusalem to Jericho and I've taken this route at least a dozen times when I've
他说有一个人从耶路撒冷去耶利哥，我走过这条路至少十几次了。

209
00:11:00,720 --> 00:11:01,280
Been in the Holy Land.
曾经在圣地。

210
00:11:01,280 --> 00:11:05,500
A certain man going from Jerusalem to Jericho and while he was going he was accosted by thieves.
有一个人从耶路撒冷去耶利哥，路上被盗贼搭讪。

211
00:11:05,500 --> 00:11:08,660
He was beaten, he was stripped naked, he was robbed, and he was left for dead.
他被殴打，他被剥光衣服，他被抢劫，他被留下等死。

212
00:11:09,640 --> 00:11:12,800
Now the text doesn't tell us anything about who did the robbing and stealing.
现在文本没有告诉我们任何关于谁进行了抢劫和偷窃的信息。

213
00:11:12,800 --> 00:11:19,180
They just mentioned this happened that there was some group of people who were willing to rob from ordinary people and try to enrich
他们只是提到这件事发生了，有一群人愿意从普通人那里抢劫并试图发财

214
00:11:19,180 --> 00:11:20,040
Themselves in this way.
自己就这样。

215
00:11:20,400 --> 00:11:25,680
And so he says this is what's going on and then he says what happened next is there was a religious man who came
所以他说这就是正在发生的事情然后他说接下来发生的是有一个宗教人士来了

216
00:11:25,680 --> 00:11:31,100
Along and he saw the man on the side of the road and instead of stopping to help he went to the other side Of the road.
一路上，他看到那个人在路边，他没有停下来帮忙，而是走到了另一边道路的。

217
00:11:31,141 --> 00:11:33,220
He ignored him and he walked on to Jericho.
他没有理睬他，径直朝耶利哥走去。

218
00:11:33,640 --> 00:11:35,780
Then there was a second religious man who came along.
然后有第二位宗教人士出现。

219
00:11:36,140 --> 00:11:37,380
He saw the man on the side of the road.
他看到了路边的那个人。

220
00:11:37,480 --> 00:11:40,180
He ignored him and he walked on the other side of the road and went on to Jericho.
他没有理睬他，而是走到路的另一边，继续前往耶利哥。

221
00:11:40,660 --> 00:11:42,480
Finally there is a third man who comes along.
最后，第三个人出现了。

222
00:11:42,620 --> 00:11:43,460
He is a Samaritan.
他是一个撒玛利亚人。

223
00:11:43,660 --> 00:11:47,480
Now just to remind you, the Samaritans and the Jews didn't get along very well at the time.
现在提醒你一下，当时撒玛利亚人和犹太人相处得不太好。

224
00:11:47,820 --> 00:11:51,120
If Jesus were telling this parable to a room filled with Democrats he'd say,
如果耶稣向满屋子的民主党人讲这个比喻，他会说：

225
00:11:51,380 --> 00:11:54,956
And there was a Republican who came along and stopped and helped the man.
有一位共和党人走过来拦住并帮助了那个人。

226
00:11:55,320 --> 00:12:01,706
If he was talking to a room filled with Republicans he'd say, and there was a Democrat who came along and stopped to help The man.
如果他正在和一个满是共和党人的房间谈话，他会说，有一个民主党人过来并停下来提供帮助那个男人。

227
00:12:01,780 --> 00:12:05,140
Or a liberal or a conservative or you pick the person who feels different from you.
或者是自由派或保守派，或者你选择感觉与你不同的人。

228
00:12:05,680 --> 00:12:05,830
Right?
正确的？

229
00:12:05,830 --> 00:12:09,658
And it was this person who came along and he saw the man and what did he do?
就是这个人过来了，他看到了那个人，他做了什么？

230
00:12:09,658 --> 00:12:10,340
He stopped and he helped him.
他停下来并帮助了他。

231
00:12:10,780 --> 00:12:11,800
He bandaged his wounds.
他包扎了伤口。

232
00:12:12,080 --> 00:12:13,140
He wrapped him in his own cloak.
他用自己的斗篷把他包裹起来。

233
00:12:13,193 --> 00:12:16,280
He put him on his own donkey, and he took him down to Jericho.
他让他骑上自己的驴，带他下到耶利哥。

234
00:12:16,280 --> 00:12:19,220
Then he provided logic for him, and he provided for his care.
然后他为他提供逻辑，并为他提供照顾。

235
00:12:20,400 --> 00:12:22,960
And Jesus said, okay, so which one was the neighbor?
耶稣说，好吧，那么谁是邻居呢？

236
00:12:23,580 --> 00:12:27,500
Who actually did what what both Moses and Jesus are teaching to do?
谁实际上做了摩西和耶稣所教导的事情？

237
00:12:27,860 --> 00:12:30,820
And of course, the legal scholar said, well, it was of course the Samaritan.
当然，法律学者说，好吧，这当然是撒玛利亚人。

238
00:12:31,440 --> 00:12:32,740
And Jesus says, go and do likewise.
耶稣说，你也去照样做吧。

239
00:12:33,180 --> 00:12:36,380
I love the fact that Dr. King preached from this text in his last sermon ever.
我喜欢金博士在他最后一次讲道中根据这段经文进行讲道的事实。

240
00:12:36,580 --> 00:12:38,671
He went to Memphis, Tennessee.
他去了田纳西州的孟菲斯。

241
00:12:38,671 --> 00:12:40,580
He was there protesting for sanitation workers.
他在那里为环卫工人抗议。

242
00:12:41,740 --> 00:12:44,420
And uh he had death threats, and he was sick when he got there.
呃，他收到了死亡威胁，而且当他到达那里时他病了。

243
00:12:44,580 --> 00:12:46,100
And he's teaching this this parable.
他正在用这个寓言来教导这一点。

244
00:12:46,480 --> 00:12:51,140
And as he's doing that, he said, you know, the question I have in my mind is like why did the two religious people
当他这样做时，他说，你知道，我脑子里的问题是为什么这两个宗教人士

245
00:12:51,140 --> 00:12:51,900
Not stop to help?
不停下来帮忙吗？

246
00:12:52,740 --> 00:12:56,143
And and he says, it's possible that they didn't maybe they were in a hurry.
他说，他们可能没有，也许他们很匆忙。

247
00:12:56,399 --> 00:12:59,320
Uh maybe they didn't stop to help because they were worried the thieves were still around,
呃，也许他们没有停下来帮忙，因为他们担心小偷还在附近，

248
00:12:59,320 --> 00:13:01,900
And the thieves would come and and attack them too.
小偷也会来攻击他们。

249
00:13:02,400 --> 00:13:02,980
So they were afraid.
所以他们害怕了。

250
00:13:03,580 --> 00:13:07,889
So they went to the outside of the road and they went on down to Jericho and left the man to die.
于是他们走到路外，继续下到耶利哥，留下那人等死。

251
00:13:07,889 --> 00:13:11,164
And they and he said, but the Samaritan, he came along, he stopped and helped.
他们和他说，但是撒玛利亚人，他过来了，他停下来帮忙。

252
00:13:11,400 --> 00:13:16,700
And he said, you know what happened was the first two religious people I'm not saying a lot of religious people do this.
他说，你知道发生的事情是前两个宗教人士，我并不是说很多宗教人士都这样做。

253
00:13:17,899 --> 00:13:21,989
So the question they asked was, what's going to happen to us if we stop and help him?
所以他们问的问题是，如果我们停下来帮助他，我们会发生什么？

254
00:13:21,989 --> 00:13:26,220
But the Samaritan asked this question, what's going to happen to him if I don't stop and help him?
但撒玛利亚人问了这个问题，如果我不停下来帮助他，他会发生什么？

255
00:13:27,299 --> 00:13:37,740
And that's the question we have to ask when we're trying to be But I do want to say there are three types of
这就是我们在努力做到这一点时必须问的问题 但我确实想说，存在三种类型

256
00:13:37,740 --> 00:13:39,283
People mentioned in this story.
这个故事里提到的人。

257
00:13:39,499 --> 00:13:43,970
There are the people who don't mind hurting other people to get to embrace themselves.
有些人不介意伤害别人来拥抱自己。

258
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:45,720
And there are some of those people in our world today.
今天我们的世界上就有这样的一些人。

259
00:13:47,140 --> 00:13:50,740
And and then there are people who know it's wrong, but they don't say anything.
还有一些人知道这是错误的，但他们什么也没说。

260
00:13:51,020 --> 00:13:52,640
They're cowardly lions, if you will.
如果你愿意的话，他们是胆怯的狮子。

261
00:13:52,999 --> 00:13:54,140
Unafraid to say anything.
什么都不怕说。

262
00:13:54,700 --> 00:13:58,000
And then there are the people like the Samaritan who stop and help.
还有像撒玛利亚人这样停下来提供帮助的人。

263
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:00,700
I just want to ask you, which one will you be?
我只想问你，你会是哪一种呢？

264
00:14:01,400 --> 00:14:02,340
Which one will I be?
我会是哪一位呢？

265
00:14:02,440 --> 00:14:04,949
Which one will the Congress be from this time forward?
从现在开始，国会将是哪一届？

266
00:14:04,959 --> 00:14:12,840
And how I got elected today.
以及我今天是如何当选的。

267
00:14:13,460 --> 00:14:15,900
I think I got elected after getting in the race just 6 months ago.
我认为我在 6 个月前参加竞选后就当选了。

268
00:14:16,040 --> 00:14:19,500
I think I got elected because Kansans were saying we're tired of the bullies.
我想我当选是因为堪萨斯人说我们厌倦了恶霸。

269
00:14:19,740 --> 00:14:21,000
We're tired of the chaos.
我们厌倦了混乱。

270
00:14:21,260 --> 00:14:27,614
We're tired of the We are no longer going to pay the pain of our neighbors.
我们厌倦了我们不再为邻居的痛苦付出代价。

271
00:14:27,614 --> 00:14:30,600
There are a lot of Kansans saying let's love our neighbors as we love ourselves.
有很多堪萨斯人说，让我们像爱自己一样爱我们的邻居。

272
00:14:30,800 --> 00:14:31,960
See, Kansans are decent people.
看吧，堪萨斯人都是正派的人。

273
00:14:32,340 --> 00:14:32,840
They're good people.
他们是好人。

274
00:14:33,020 --> 00:14:33,430
They're pragmatic.
他们很务实。

275
00:14:33,430 --> 00:14:34,689
They care about each other.
他们互相关心。

276
00:14:34,960 --> 00:14:36,576
That's who we are in Kansas.
这就是我们在堪萨斯州的情况。

277
00:14:36,940 --> 00:14:38,260
Now, I want to mention just one more word.
现在，我想再提一句。

278
00:14:38,880 --> 00:14:40,200
I'm a United Methodist pastor.
我是联合卫理公会的牧师。

279
00:14:40,301 --> 00:14:43,991
I've been a United Methodist pastor for 40 years, nearly 40 years.
我担任联合卫理公会牧师已经四十年了，快四十年了。

280
00:14:43,991 --> 00:14:45,940
We have this vision statement in the United Methodist Church.
我们在联合卫理公会有这样的愿景声明。

281
00:14:46,200 --> 00:14:47,920
We put it on a coffee mug at Church of the Resurrection.
我们把它放在复活教堂的咖啡杯上。

282
00:14:47,920 --> 00:14:51,940
It says, and I love this, it's it just tells you a little bit about our denomination,
它说，我喜欢这个，它只是告诉你一些关于我们教派的信息，

283
00:14:52,111 --> 00:14:56,360
But it also is just a good cry for every human being, whether you're a person of faith or not.
但这对每个人来说也是一个美好的呼喊，无论你是否有信仰。

284
00:14:56,801 --> 00:14:57,600
This is what we're called to do.
这就是我们蒙召要做的事。

285
00:14:57,780 --> 00:15:02,880
Love boldly, serve joyfully, and lead courageously.
大胆地爱，快乐地服务，勇敢地领导。

286
00:15:04,220 --> 00:15:09,920
I was preaching a sermon series on that on those three things in last October when I began feeling this sense of okay,
去年十月，当我开始感到这种感觉良好时，我正在就这三件事进行系列讲道，

287
00:15:10,020 --> 00:15:14,380
What does it look like for you, preacher, to love boldly, to serve joyfully,
传道人，勇敢地去爱，喜乐地服务，对你来说是什么样子的？

288
00:15:14,520 --> 00:15:15,420
And to lead courageously?
并勇敢地领导？

289
00:15:16,140 --> 00:15:21,585
And I couldn't get out of my mind that maybe that meant running for the United States Senate.
我一直在想，也许这意味着竞选美国参议员。

290
00:15:21,595 --> 00:15:31,123
I want to thank you, the people of Kansas who voted for me,
我要感谢投票给我的堪萨斯人民

291
00:15:31,123 --> 00:15:33,560
All of those of you who volunteered and worked so hard.
你们所有自愿并努力工作的人。

292
00:15:33,560 --> 00:15:34,280
You put signs up.
你贴上标语。

293
00:15:34,540 --> 00:15:35,131
You made calls.
你打过电话。

294
00:15:35,131 --> 00:15:36,005
You knocked on doors.
你敲了门。

295
00:15:36,060 --> 00:15:36,560
You gave.
你给了。

296
00:15:36,560 --> 00:15:37,640
You contributed to my campaign.
你为我的竞选活动做出了贡献。

297
00:15:37,680 --> 00:15:38,760
You told all of your friends.
你告诉了你所有的朋友。

298
00:15:39,120 --> 00:15:40,420
I would not be here were it not for you.
如果没有你，我就不会在这里。

299
00:15:40,520 --> 00:15:41,220
I work for you.
我为你工作。

300
00:15:41,460 --> 00:15:42,720
I'm going to represent you.
我来代表你。

301
00:15:43,160 --> 00:15:50,740
And all of these people and those people who did not vote for me,
所有这些人和那些没有投票给我的人，

302
00:15:50,740 --> 00:15:52,460
You know, I'm going to represent them, too.
你知道，我也将代表他们。

303
00:15:52,780 --> 00:15:53,480
I care about them.
我关心他们。

304
00:15:53,480 --> 00:15:55,060
I saw a guy at a coffee shop this week.
这周我在一家咖啡店见到了一个人。

305
00:15:55,060 --> 00:15:55,940
He said I didn't vote for you.
他说我没有投票给你。

306
00:15:55,962 --> 00:15:57,738
I was afraid the Democrats would take control of the Senate.
我担心民主党会控制参议院。

307
00:15:57,738 --> 00:15:58,120
Well, guess what?
嗯，你猜怎么着？

308
00:15:58,360 --> 00:15:59,540
They're going to take control of the Senate.
他们将控制参议院。

309
00:16:09,301 --> 00:16:16,606
Because this election, this election is a rebuke of unkindness and cruelty in Washington, D.C.
因为这次选举，这次选举是对华盛顿不仁慈和残忍的谴责，华盛顿特区

310
00:16:16,956 --> 00:16:20,800
So, I'm going to thank all of you.
所以，我要感谢你们所有人。

311
00:16:20,800 --> 00:16:21,940
I want to thank Shelly Pets.
我要感谢雪莉宠物。

312
00:16:22,100 --> 00:16:25,166
I know she's around here somewhere, and she led a team who were my prayer partners,
我知道她就在附近的某个地方，她领导的团队是我的祈祷伙伴，

313
00:16:25,360 --> 00:16:29,780
And they prayed for me every day, and I just can't tell you I felt when I had somebody call me,
他们每天都为我祈祷，我无法告诉你当有人打电话给我时我的感受，

314
00:16:29,980 --> 00:16:31,260
You know, a groomer.
你知道，美容师。

315
00:16:31,260 --> 00:16:36,840
I mean, you know, you had the President of the United States come to Kansas City and and to Wichita and to Kansas twice
我的意思是，你知道，美国总统曾两次访问堪萨斯城、威奇托和堪萨斯州

316
00:16:36,840 --> 00:16:39,300
In two weeks to to, you know, to talk smack about me.
两周后，你知道，就会谈论我。

317
00:16:39,540 --> 00:16:42,419
And the Vice President to do the same thing and to say I wasn't really a Christian.
副总统也做了同样的事情，并说我不是真正的基督徒。

318
00:16:42,680 --> 00:16:43,040
But you know what?
但你知道吗？

319
00:16:43,120 --> 00:16:45,079
I didn't feel any of that.
我对此没有任何感觉。

320
00:16:45,079 --> 00:16:49,252
I just felt like little arrows just fell to the ground.
我只觉得小箭掉到了地上。

321
00:16:50,021 --> 00:16:56,814
And in part that was because of Shelly and her team and all of you who were praying for lobotomy.
部分原因是雪莉和她的团队以及所有人为脑白质切除术祈祷。

322
00:16:57,210 --> 00:16:59,990
We just felt such peace in the middle of this from your prayers.
在你们的祈祷中，我们感到如此平静。

323
00:17:00,350 --> 00:17:01,150
So I want to thank you for that.
所以我想为此感谢你。

324
00:17:01,490 --> 00:17:04,770
I want to thank my amazing uh team of staff.
我要感谢我出色的呃团队。

325
00:17:04,970 --> 00:17:18,940
Would you all raise your hands my staff I love this.
你们都举手吗，我的员工，我喜欢这个。

326
00:17:18,940 --> 00:17:19,090
And I'm about done.
我快完成了。

327
00:17:19,090 --> 00:17:21,400
You know, a preacher says that about 10 times.
你知道，一位牧师说过大约十次这样的话。

328
00:17:21,420 --> 00:17:21,980
I'm about done.
我快完成了。

329
00:17:22,952 --> 00:17:26,945
But uh but I remember 6 months ago when we got the race and the Cook report said,
但是呃，但是我记得 6 个月前，当我们参加比赛时，库克报告说，

330
00:17:27,195 --> 00:17:28,442
Now Kansas is solidly red.
现在堪萨斯州已经完全变成红色了。

331
00:17:28,560 --> 00:17:36,068
There's no chance they're going to elect a Democrat And then about a month and a half later they said,
他们不可能选举民主党人然后大约一个半月后他们说，

332
00:17:36,068 --> 00:17:36,800
Well, they're likely red.
嗯，它们可能是红色的。

333
00:17:37,480 --> 00:17:39,360
And then a month and a half later they said, well, they lean red.
一个半月后，他们说，好吧，他们变红了。

334
00:17:39,543 --> 00:17:41,460
And then 3 weeks later they said, oh, well, you know, it's a toss up.
三周后，他们说，哦，好吧，你知道，这是一个折腾。

335
00:17:41,900 --> 00:17:46,740
Well, that's because in part these staff who gave themselves worked tirelessly to make this happen.
嗯，部分原因是这些员工为实现这一目标而付出了不懈的努力。

336
00:17:48,972 --> 00:17:59,937
I do want to single out one person because this would have never happened were it not for my campaign manager, Mike Fultz.
我确实想挑出一个人，因为如果没有我的竞选经理，这一切都不会发生，迈克·富尔茨。

337
00:17:59,937 --> 00:18:00,420
Where are you, Mike?
迈克，你在哪里？

338
00:18:00,762 --> 00:18:09,100
It would never have happened without him.
没有他，这一切都不会发生。

339
00:18:10,100 --> 00:18:13,940
I want to thank the people of my congregation, the United Methodist Church of the Resurrection.
我要感谢我的会众，联合卫理公会复活教堂的人们。

340
00:18:14,200 --> 00:18:22,040
I am We made sure that we had careful separations and all that kind of stuff,
我是 我们确保我们进行了仔细的分离以及诸如此类的事情，

341
00:18:22,040 --> 00:18:27,260
But I am so proud of who you are as a congregation, and I'm so grateful that you gave me a leave of absence
但我为你们作为一个会众感到非常自豪，我很感激你们给我请假

342
00:18:27,260 --> 00:18:29,480
To pursue what I believe was a calling from God.
追求我认为是来自上帝的召唤。

343
00:18:29,600 --> 00:18:34,020
I still believe it was a calling from God to try to make a difference in our world in a different kind of way,
我仍然相信这是上帝的召唤，试图以不同的方式改变我们的世界，

344
00:18:34,020 --> 00:18:37,860
And I just thank you so much for for just allowing me to do this.
我非常感谢您允许我这样做。

345
00:18:42,015 --> 00:18:43,893
I'm so proud.
我很自豪。

346
00:18:43,893 --> 00:18:48,700
And my family and all of my friends who have come alongside us and just cheered us on and encouraged us,
我的家人和所有和我们一起为我们加油、鼓励我们的朋友，

347
00:18:48,880 --> 00:18:50,240
We would not be here without you.
没有你，我们就不会在这里。

348
00:18:50,680 --> 00:18:57,180
Tonight we made history, but the real work starts January 3rd.
今晚我们创造了历史，但真正的工作要从 1 月 3 日开始。

349
00:18:59,058 --> 00:19:01,978
I want to invite you to join me.
我想邀请你加入我。

350
00:19:02,708 --> 00:19:05,628
I'm going to try to do this in the Senate.
我将尝试在参议院做到这一点。

351
00:19:05,840 --> 00:19:07,020
I figure I got six years.
我想我还有六年的时间。

352
00:19:07,160 --> 00:19:11,911
I'm going to do all I can to love boldly and help us as a nation love boldly,
我将尽我所能去大胆地去爱，并帮助我们作为一个勇敢地去爱的国家，

353
00:19:11,911 --> 00:19:16,733
To serve joyfully, and to lead courageously.
快乐服务，勇敢领导。

354
00:19:16,743 --> 00:19:21,510
Thank you so much for being here.
非常感谢您来到这里。

355
00:19:21,750 --> 00:19:25,743
I am so proud to represent you in the United States Senate.
我很自豪能够在美国参议院代表你们。

356
00:19:25,743 --> 00:19:30,843
God bless you and God bless [unclear].
愿上帝保佑你们，也愿上帝保佑[听不清]。
